Package: meshedghs
Type: Package
Title: Adaptive Borrowing Across Misaligned Outcomes in Meshed Gaussian Process Coregionalization Models
Version: 0.1.3
Date: 2026-09-17
Authors@R: c(
    person("Sagnik", "Bhadury", email = "sagnik.bhadury@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = "design-based grouped horseshoe prior, its updates under parameter expansion, and the user interface"),
    person("Michele", "Peruzzi", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = "author and copyright holder of the 'meshed' package (version 0.2.3, GPL >= 3), from which the meshed Gaussian process sampler is derived; not involved in the development of this package"))
Description: Bayesian multivariate spatial and space-depth regression for misaligned outcomes, in which
    a design-based grouped horseshoe prior on the off-diagonal loadings of a linear model of
    coregionalization lets each outcome borrow from a block of other outcomes only when the data
    support it. The prior is specified on the identified loadings under the parameter expansion used for
    posterior sampling, and the local and global scales are sampled exactly from discretized full
    conditionals. The latent factors are meshed Gaussian processes, and the blocked Gibbs sampler is derived
    from the 'meshed' package of Peruzzi, Banerjee and Finley (2022) <doi:10.1080/01621459.2020.1833889>,
    Peruzzi, Banerjee, Dunson and Finley (2025) <doi:10.1214/25-BA1515> and Peruzzi and Dunson (2024),
    whose functions are retained. With no groups supplied, the package reproduces 'meshed' 0.2.3.
License: GPL (>= 3)
URL: https://github.com/sagnikbhadury/meshedghs
